  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). PARTLY MISPREMISED (code/row read). Axiom half current: ADR-0050 §1 (:71-85) and the registry axiom (io_boundary_types.py:4-9) unchanged; content-reading rows elixir.yaml:249-258, erlang.yaml:315, javascript.yaml:295-297 (cookie), :298-307 (location); navigation_read's chooser definition io_boundary_types.py:399-413; 'logging names a medium' :324-329. Scope wider: env_read's OWN definition is by content ('values that may carry a credential', :235-238) and host_info_read by identity (:247-250), so the amendment must address the INV-tutar split itself, not only rows. The Unix-socket comparison was wrong: it set C's AF_UNIX send rows against go dial/listen (go.yaml:262 DialUnix, :376 ListenUnix), but C's own connect() is also net_send (c.yaml:157-162), and WI-potog (PR #1417) kept go dial/listen to that precedent and moved go writes/reads (fmt.Fprint*, io.WriteString, bufio) to ipc. Remaining socket cases: go net.Conn.Write/Read = WI-kalol; python asyncio.StreamReader = WI-foloh; untracked, now owned here: python socket.socket.send/recv over AF_UNIX (python.yaml:610-611) and node net.Socket (javascript.yaml:163-164). asyncio.start_unix_server (python.yaml:749, net_listen) cannot be fixed by a row edit: there is no ipc-side listen value, so it needs a vocabulary ruling. swift.yaml:181-183 'argv is env_read in every catalogue' is false (go has no os.Args row); it goes with WI-zidam. OWNER RULING 2026-10-25 (via WI-zidam's cookie route): the amendment is NOT 'the value names only the medium'. It says: a row's primary boundary names the MEDIUM; a `simultaneous` second boundary may record the reading a taint label needs (credential-bearing; chosen by the party that navigated), as the shipped INV-dadu URL rows already do. It must state outright that env_read therefore still means both the process environment and 'may carry a credential'. Lands before WI-zidam (isbefore added). P3 kept."  # abaf
